    },
    "**%@** takes the huyền tone: start low and let it fall gently. It sounded like **%@**." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "**%@** takes the hỏi tone: dip down, then come back up. It sounded like **%@**." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "**%@** takes the ngã tone: rise with a little catch in the throat. It sounded like **%@**." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "**%@** takes the nặng tone: drop low and cut it short. It sounded like **%@**." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "**%@** takes the sắc tone: start mid, then rise sharply. It sounded like **%@**." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual"
    },
    "**%@**: đ is a firm “d”, while d sounds like “z” (north) or “y” (south). It sounded like **%@**." : {
